[gd_scene format=3 uid="uid://unitdirshadowsharedatlas"]

; Moves the atlas share. Two orthogonal suns each take half the atlas's width at its full height, so
; the thin posts cast nothing across the halved width, while the bars cast as under one sun. In every
; other golden at most one sun takes a share, the whole atlas, so a light that ignores its share is
; invisible there. Both suns end at 60 units, which sets the texel size the widths step through.

